-- | What a piece of [`crate::Trivia`] is.
-- |
-- | Plan 02 (`docs/07 - 02 - Lexical Surface.md`), leaf 3 extends plan 01's two
-- | variants with the doc-comment and fence forms of doc 03 §4.1.
-- |
-- | Doc comments are **trivia, not tokens**. They attach to the item they
-- | precede exactly as ordinary comments do, so plan 23 can translate them to
-- | `///` and `//!` without the grammar knowing they exist. Emerald made the
-- | opposite choice — a `doc: Option<String>` field on six AST node kinds — and
-- | its formatter can round-trip only those six, losing every other comment.
-- | Trivia is the general mechanism; a field on a node is the special case.
export data TriviaKind
  -- | `--` — an ordinary comment, on its own line or trailing code. The stored
  -- | text excludes the `--` and one optional following space.
  -- |
  -- | Doc 18 §5.1 changed the marker from `#` to `--`, which emptied `#` of
  -- | four of its six meanings and made the longest-match table a line. These
  -- | four doc comments named the old markers until plan 23 noticed — the
  -- | scanners were converted and their documentation was not.
  = LineComment
  -- | `-- |` — an outer doc comment, becoming `///`. Haddock's own marker.
  | DocComment
  -- | `-- !` — an inner doc comment, becoming `//!`. Doc 18 §5.1's own
  -- | invention, since Haskell has no module-level analogue of `//!`; it
  -- | echoes Rust's `/`-to-`!` step.
  | InnerDocComment
  -- | `{- … -}` — a fenced multi-line comment, becoming `/* … */`. The stored
  -- | text is the body between the fences.
  | FencedComment
  -- | `#[…]` — an outer attribute, copied through verbatim (doc 03 §13.2).
  -- |
  -- | **Trivia and not an item**, which is plan 18 §1.3's whole design. An
  -- | attribute is not a declaration — `#[inline]` does not stand alone — and
  -- | trivia is Redox's mechanism for text that belongs to a construct without
  -- | being one. Joining it keeps source order with comments, reaches every
  -- | item kind and every statement at once, and inherits doc 02 §10.1's rule
  -- | that trivia survives into the `.xrs`.
  -- |
  -- | The stored text excludes `#[` and `]`, as the token's does: an inner
  -- | attribute needs different brackets, so the emitter writes them.
  | Attribute
  -- | `#![…]` — an inner attribute.
  -- |
  -- | Emitted **in place**. Rust requires inner attributes to precede every
  -- | other item, so one written halfway down a file lands halfway down the
  -- | `.xrs` and rustc objects — which plan 18 §1.4 chooses deliberately over
  -- | gathering them to the top, because gathering is a reordering and plan 14
  -- | decision 3 declined those without cause.
  | InnerAttribute
  -- | A run of one or more blank lines. The run's length is not recorded,
  -- | because the emitter collapses any run to a single blank line and nothing
  -- | in the language depends on the count.
  | BlankLines
  deriving (Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)

instance TriviaKind
  -- | Whether this trivium carries documentation, which the emitter renders as
  -- | `///` or `//!` rather than `//`.
  export is_doc : &self -> bool
  is_doc self = case self of
    DocComment or InnerDocComment -> true
    _ -> false
